## Troubleshooting Checklist

| Issue | Check |
|-------|-------|
| Inbound calls not arriving | Verify DNID is bound to the application AND the application routes to the inbound trunk in cockpit.cloudonix.io |
| "Trunk not found" / 404 | Ensure **Allowed Addresses** in LiveKit includes Cloudonix's full egress IP list |
| 401 / 407 on outbound | Confirm Username/Password are LEFT EMPTY (Cloudonix uses service-provider trust, not digest) |
| Outbound calls fail with no obvious error | Confirm LiveKit support has provisioned Cloudonix as a service-provider on your project — without this, outbound will not work no matter what config you use |
| One-way audio | Confirm UDP/RTP ports are open in your cloud firewall and `use_external_ip: true` is set in `livekit-sip` config if behind NAT |
| No room created | Check dispatch rule is linked to the correct trunk ID |
| Wrong outbound host | Use the exact host LiveKit support gave you — do NOT use the `<uuid>.sip.cloudonix.net` inbound alias |

