## Quick Reference: Configuration Summary

**Cloudonix Side:**
```
Cockpit (cockpit.cloudonix.io):
  → Inbound Trunk: <uuid>.sip.cloudonix.net (auto-issued)
  → Application: routes incoming calls to inbound trunk
  → DNID Numbers: bound to application

Authentication:
  → API layer: bearer token (not used by LiveKit)
  → SIP layer: service-provider trust (no digest)

Outbound Provisioning:
  → Discord ticket to LiveKit support
  → 24-48h lead time
  → LiveKit provides the outbound SIP host
```

**LiveKit Side:**
```
Inbound Trunk:
  → Name: Cloudonix Inbound
  → Number Format: +E.164 (WITH +)
  → Numbers: Your Cloudonix DNID
  → Allowed Addresses: Cloudonix egress IP list
  → Auth: None

Dispatch Rule:
  → Linked to: Cloudonix Inbound trunk
  → Type: Direct/Individual/Multi-Line (your choice)
  → Agent: Your AI agent

Outbound Trunk (only after LiveKit provisions):
  → Name: Cloudonix Outbound
  → Address: [host provided by LiveKit support]
  → Transport: UDP
  → Number Format: +E.164 (WITH +)
  → Auth: None (service-provider trust)
  → Numbers: Your Cloudonix DNID
```

